	"note": "defence is the town's own wall (battles.md section 9): a town is a company with a wall, and it has one before it builds anything. It lives here rather than in a battle table because the town hall is the building every town has from the moment it is founded, which makes it the anchor for town-wide effects, and because a defence figure authored anywhere but beside the thing that defends is a second place that thing is described. The figure is tuning. Its upkeep is zero, so unlike the defence branch this wall can never go dark.",
